      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T22:23:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the core of what this is doing is good, but I think it can be simpler and avoid the lock juggling. \n\n(Specifically, you are doing a more correct thing by accounting against the old_rq nr_uninterruptible, but the nr_uninterruptible accounting is sort of unbalanced anyway, since its usually dec\u0027ed against the rq it is joining, not the one it was removed from (where it was inc\u0027ed - so I\u0027m not sure that\u0027s needed). \n\nSee my take here: https://r.android.com/4179535",
      "revId": "4e7a29eeecf0d82381463fbadea04ff74882cc48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cffcb388_d1d116b3",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7370,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T22:23:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this looks reasonable on its face, but nr_iowait and nr_uninterruptible track tasks that are not on the runqueue. With proxy_migrate() we are migrating tasks from one rq to another, so they should not have any bearing on the nr_iowait or nr_uninterruptible values.  So I don\u0027t believe this is necessary.",
      "revId": "4e7a29eeecf0d82381463fbadea04ff74882cc48",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
